In article <1991Mar4.160040.1003@cunixf.cc.columbia.edu>, eh@cunixb.cc.columbia.edu (Erik Hilsdale) writes:
> recently i posted the idea that nethack 3.1 should be
> user-configurable for screen size in order to get
> larger level sizes for those who have spiffier
> terminals.

I like this.  Many years ago, when I `colorized' PC Hack 3.0 (Turner
hadn't made it a dirty word yet) my makesfiles could produce either
a normal 80x24 or an EGA-only 80x43.  Everyone who I knew played these
preferred the 43-line.  Not because each level had more loot or monsters,
but because the levels were far more complicated and interesting, 
architecturally.  Oh, and the grid squares were closer to squares.

I really think levels should be variable-sized.  If needed, the initial
probability tables of objects and monsters can be adjusted at startup.

